From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:31:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: Support hostless voice call
 graphs (WIP)

Local bring-up work to run the vendor voice call graph (VCPM, mailboxes,
Fluence ECNS) generated from the device's ACDB:

- module configuration arrays from the topology for any module, by kind:
  set-config, persistent (registered through shared memory, e.g. VCPM
  calibration tables), extra graph-open parameters (control links,
  VCPM voice config), late set-config (VCPM cal keys) and links to the
  playback device graph; parameters the DSP rejects are reported and
  skipped
- hostless FE graphs (no shared memory endpoint): only the topology
  configuration, then prepare and start
- sub-graph VSID property (don't care), which VCPM uses to find the
  sub-graphs of a voice session
- graph open out of band when it exceeds the in-band GPR limit, and
  graph open failures are reported instead of ignored
- shared memory addresses carry the SMMU stream ID like the data buffers
- a debugfs file (q6apm_raw) to send raw APM commands, bring-up only

Status: the full graph opens and starts, but the modem never attaches
a voice session to VCPM yet.
